// Golden eval set — one JSON object per line. Blank lines and // comments are ignored.
//
// This file is empty. `eval` and `calibrate` do nothing useful until you add
// items, and the CI quality gate has nothing to gate on. Build it early: it is
// what turns "the answer looked fine" into a number that can regress.
//
// FIELDS
//   id                  short stable name, shown in `eval -verbose` output
//   query               the question, phrased the way a real user would
//   relevant_chunk_ids  chunk ids that genuinely answer it (from `chunks -dir`)
//   gold_answer         optional; enables citation + answer-correctness scoring
//   stage               optional; retrieval | rerank | generation — tags which
//                       stage the item exercises, so a regression can be
//                       attributed instead of merely observed
//   acl                 optional; permission tags to retrieve under
//
// Chunk ids are the contract. They change whenever chunking changes, so
// re-run `./ask-my-docs chunks -dir corpus` and update them after touching
// MAX_CHUNK_CHARS, CHUNK_OVERLAP, or the documents themselves.
//
// WHAT TO COVER — a set that only asks easy questions cannot detect anything:
//   - exact identifiers (error codes, SKUs, part numbers) — exercises the
//     sparse/lexical retrieval leg, which is what pure vector search gets wrong
//   - paraphrases sharing no words with the source — exercises the dense leg
//   - two chunks on the same topic where only one answers — exercises reranking
//   - questions your corpus genuinely cannot answer, with
//     "relevant_chunk_ids": [] — exercises the confidence gate. Without at
//     least one of these, `calibrate` cannot bound the gate from below.
//
// Aim for enough items that one flipping does not move the mean much: at 13
// items scored in 0/0.5/1.0 steps, a single item is worth 0.038.
//
// EXAMPLES (delete these — the ids are made up and will not match your corpus):
//
// {"id": "refund-window", "query": "How long do I have to request a refund?", "relevant_chunk_ids": ["billing.md#2"], "gold_answer": "Within 90 days of the invoice date.", "stage": "generation"}
// {"id": "err-4290", "query": "ERR-4290", "relevant_chunk_ids": ["api-errors.md#1"], "stage": "retrieval"}
// {"id": "out-of-corpus", "query": "What is the parental leave policy?", "relevant_chunk_ids": [], "gold_answer": "I don't have enough information in the indexed documents to answer that.", "stage": "generation"}
